-- title:
--   Level lowering at q from a K₁(qᵃ)-fixed vector
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a natural number and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a normalized eigenform in the sense of the project's predicate: its width-one $q$-expansion satisfies $a_1(g)=1$, $a_{mn}(g)=a_m(g)a_n(g)$ for coprime $m,n$, the recursion $a_{p^{r+2}}(g)=a_p(g)a_{p^{r+1}}(g)-p\,a_{p^r}(g)$ for primes $p\nmid M$, and $a_{p^{r+2}}(g)=a_p(g)a_{p^{r+1}}(g)$ for primes $p\mid M$. Let $q$ be a prime, and let $\Phi$ be a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of $\mathbb{Q}$ which is an adelic lift of $g$: $\Phi$ is left invariant under the global points $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$, right invariant under the finite level-one subgroup attached to the ideal $(M)$, and at every adelic matrix $h$ with trivial finite component and archimedean component in $\mathrm{GL}_2^+(\mathbb{R})$ one has $\Phi(h)=(g\mid_2 h_\infty)(i)$. Let $a$ be a natural number and let $y$ be an element of the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the adelic translates of $\Phi$ which (i) lies in the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-translates of the distinguished vector $\Phi$ itself, (ii) is nonzero, (iii) is fixed by every element of the congruence subgroup $K_1(q^a)\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$, and (iv) is fixed by every scalar matrix $\mathrm{diag}(z,z)$ with $z\in\mathbb{Q}_q^\times$. Then the eigensystem of $g$ occurs at level $M/q^{v_q(M)-a}$ (natural-number subtraction and division): there is a normalized eigenform $h$ of weight two on $\Gamma_0\bigl(M/q^{v_q(M)-a}\bigr)$ with $a_\ell(h)=a_\ell(g)$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$.
--
--   This is the level-lowering step of local newvector theory in adelic form: the existence of a nonzero vector in the local $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-span of an adelic lift which is fixed by $K_1(q^a)$ and by the centre forces the Hecke eigensystem away from $M$ to be realised already at the level whose $q$-exponent is lowered to $a$. It is used in the determination of the conductor of the local component at $q$ of the representation generated by a newform's adelic lift.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_IsNormalizedEigenform_goodEigensystemOccursAt_of_adelicLift_of_mem_span_of_fixed.lean

